<BaseLayout title="GB21 (Jianjing) — Shoulder Well Point" description="Learn how to locate and stimulate GB21 (Jianjing) — the Shoulder Well point on the upper trapezius. Benefits include shoulder tension relief, neck pain relief, and headache prevention." articleSchema={true}>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 lg:px-6">
    <h1 class="mb-4">GB21 (Jianjing) — Shoulder Well</h1>
    <p class="text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400 text-lg mb-8">GB21, known as Jianjing or Shoulder Well, is the primary point for releasing shoulder and neck tension. Located on the top of the shoulder, it is a go-to point for desk workers and those with chronic tightness.</p>

    <section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">Location</h2>
    <img src="/images/gb21-location.png" alt="GB21 acupressure point location on the top of the shoulder" class="w-full max-w-sm mx-auto rounded-xl shadow-sm" />
    <p class="mb-3">GB21 is on the top of the shoulder, midway between the spinous process of the seventh cervical vertebra (C7 ?the prominent bone at the base of the neck) and the acromion (the tip of the shoulder).</p>

    </section><section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">Benefits &amp; Uses</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-3 space-y-1 text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">
      <li><strong>Shoulder tension:</strong> GB21 releases tightness in the trapezius and levator scapulae muscles.</li>
      <li><strong>Neck stiffness:</strong> It improves range of motion in the neck and relieves cervical tension.</li>
      <li><strong>Headaches:</strong> GB21 helps with tension headaches originating from shoulder and neck tightness.</li>
      <li><strong>Stress relief:</strong> Stimulating GB21 releases physical tension stored in the shoulders from stress.</li>
      <li><strong>Arm and elbow pain:</strong> It can help with referred pain patterns down the arm from shoulder tension.</li>
    </ul>

    </section><section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">How to Massage GB21</h2>
    <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 space-y-2 text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">
      <li>Use the thumb of one hand to reach across to the opposite shoulder.</li>
      <li>Locate GB21 at the highest point of the shoulder muscle.</li>
      <li>Apply firm pressure with your thumb in a kneading or circular motion.</li>
      <li>Hold for 30?0 seconds while breathing deeply.</li>
      <li>Repeat on the other shoulder. For best results, have a partner assist.</li>
    </ol>

    </section><section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">Science &amp; Research</h2>
    <p class="mb-3">A 2020 randomized trial in <em>Journal of Physical Therapy Science</em> found that GB21 acupressure significantly reduced neck and shoulder pain in office workers compared to a control group.<sup><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32275103/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">1</a></sup> Research in <em>Acupuncture in Medicine</em> demonstrated that GB21 stimulation increased blood flow to the shoulder muscles and reduced muscle tension measured by EMG.<sup><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30949292/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">2</a></sup></p>
    <p class="mb-3">A 2021 systematic review in <em>Complementary Therapies in Clinical Practice</em> confirmed that GB21 is one of the most effective points for treating myofascial pain syndrome of the upper trapezius.<sup><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34284274/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">3</a></sup></p>

    </section><section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">Precautions</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-3 space-y-1 text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">
      <li><strong>Avoid during pregnancy:</strong> GB21 is contraindicated in pregnancy as it may stimulate uterine contractions.</li>
      <li>Use caution if you have a recent shoulder injury, rotator cuff tear, or shoulder surgery.</li>
      <li>Do not apply pressure over broken skin, moles, or skin lesions on the shoulder.</li>
      <li>Stop if pressure causes numbness or tingling radiating down the arm.</li>
    </ul>

    </section><section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">Related Points</h2>
    <p class="mb-3">GB21 pairs well with <a href="/points/gb20-fengchi-acupressure-point">GB20 (Fengchi)</a> for comprehensive neck and shoulder relief. For tension headaches, combine with <a href="/points/li4-hegu-acupressure-point">LI4 (Hegu)</a> and <a href="/points/gb20-fengchi-acupressure-point">GB20</a>.</p>
  </section></article>
